            <p><strong>a)</strong> $\int \sqrt{x}(x + 5x^3)\,dx = \int (x^{\frac{3}{2}} + 5x^{\frac{7}{2}})\,dx = \frac{2}{5}x^2\sqrt{x} + \frac{10}{9}x^4\sqrt{x} + C$</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p><strong>b)</strong> $\int \frac{4x + 5x^6}{2\sqrt{x}}\,dx = \int \left(2x^{\frac{1}{2}} + \frac{5}{2}x^{\frac{11}{2}}\right)dx = \frac{4}{3}x\sqrt{x} + \frac{5}{13}x^6\sqrt{x} + C$</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p><strong>c)</strong> $\int 5^x \cdot 4^x\,dx = \int 20^x\,dx = \frac{20^x}{\ln 20} + C$</p>
          </div>
